  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,\u27f9\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,\u27f9\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,\u27f9\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e8-75,40,-5\u27e9.$",
